{"id":"n989da55803","headline":"NSE cuts IPO price range, giving up shot at India’s top listing","summary":"The National Stock Exchange of India is likely to price its IPO at Rs 1,700-1,785 a share, below its earlier Rs 2,000-2,100 range. It may cut the stake on offer to 5.5%, valuing it at up to 4.42 trillion rupees.","why":"The NSE is India's largest stock exchange by volume. Its listing would be among the country's biggest IPOs and sets a valuation benchmark for exchange operators.","category":"companies","event_type":"capital","importance":2,"flag":null,"market_moving":false,"location":{"place":"Mumbai","country":"India","lat":19.08,"lon":72.88,"region":"asia"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"The Economic Times","url":"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/ipos/fpos/nse-set-to-price-india-ipo-at-rs-1700-to-rs-1785-a-share/articleshow/133935920.cms"},"sources":[{"name":"The Economic Times","url":"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/ipos/fpos/nse-set-to-price-india-ipo-at-rs-1700-to-rs-1785-a-share/articleshow/133935920.cms"}],"published_at":"2026-09-08T17:40:00Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-12T08:33:11Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"288642b10cee54e5","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-12T08:33:11Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-09-08T17:40:00Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-09-08T18:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"IN","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/stock-exchange-building-2463798.jpg","alt":"stock exchange building (illustration)","credit":"AhmadArdity","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/stock-trading-financial-finance-2463798/"}}